          %h2#lambekscott_indecomposability Lambek–Scott indecomposability
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Higher-Order+Categorical+Logic"} Lambek Scott
            give a different definition of indecomposability. Generalizing their definition slightly, we may say that an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong indecomposable
            (in the sense of Lambek–Scott) if any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jointly+epimorphic+family"} jointly epimorphic family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}_i
            of arrows into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            contains at least one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↠
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \twoheadrightarrow X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to X
            is not epic (this to ensure that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            is not indecomposable).
          %p
            If the epi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ↠
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \twoheadrightarrow X
            is required to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
            the Lambek–Scott definition implies that given above: if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \colon X \cong \coprod_i U_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
