          %h2#irreducible Indecomposability vs irreducibility
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+representation"} indecomposable representation
            is precisely an indecomposable object in an appropriate category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rep
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible representation
            is precisely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+object"} simple object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep
          %p
            However, one level
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorified"} decategorified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+element"} irreducible element
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is precisely an indecomposable object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            when thought of as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+category"} thin category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+element"} atomic element
            = succeed "-simple.)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          %p The bottom line is that ‘irreducible’ and ‘indecomposable’ sometimes mean the same thing but sometimes don't, and ‘irreducible’ doesn't even mean the same thing across different fields.
